#!/bin/bash
# DIAGNOSTIC (not an experiment): the manual's procedure for choosing a nounif
# (manual 6.7.2: "one typically uses set verboseRules = true. to display the
# clauses generated by ProVerif").  Short box, output truncated on disk.
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
f="$1"; n="${f%.pv}"; box="${2:-300}"
echo "# DIAG START $(date -u +%FT%TZ) $n box=${box}s" >> abl.log
( ulimit -v 10485760; nice -n 19 timeout "$box" \
    proverif -lib ../../../../lib/tessera_theory.pvl "$f" 2>&1 | head -c 2000000000 > "$n.out" )
echo "# DIAG END $(date -u +%FT%TZ) $n bytes=$(stat -c%s "$n.out")" >> abl.log
